{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact orphan-retirement report head 4dc114540ee27de276572c72505cef19020f02db for request #10141 (git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:167a8ae6b87463ad449fccd808e91eb5289fce1d). Both exact artifacts were inspected; notes/deploy-spike.md is primary.\n\nThe evidence supports the requested retirement. I read the full before/after Worker and container listings and four deletion receipts supplied under effective assertion #10359, at /tmp/artroom-builder-orphans-f77ebf20/. Exactly artroom-spike-isogit and artroom-spike-sandbox-git disappear from the Worker list; all other listed Workers remain with unchanged recorded timestamps. The two removed container applications are artroom-lb-logbig-publisher (9cf9349e) and artroom-spike-sandbox-git-gitbox (60795e20); the Room publisher and checker runner remain. The report records each deleted Worker's last version ID. Source/config inspection confirms that the surviving Room and checker service do not bind to those four resources, and the sandbox-git source/results remain in the repository.\n\nThe prior 404-based health claim is withdrawn. The committed 02:23 UTC smoke record supplies actual post-deletion runtime evidence: all 32 steps pass; the Room dispatches through its checker service binding and admits the machine-run check at seq 9 after 10.427 seconds; the independent review follows; the landing completes; the log publishes through 15; the recorded verifier exits 0 with four policy decisions replayed and no failures. The fixture's imported repository and workspace fork are both listed in cleanup, with no repositories left and no unresolved duties. The record also preserves verify's stated proof limits. These are independently examined records of builder's run, not a live run I performed.\n\nAuthority and scope are explicit. Planner's effective operator request follows Hugh's decision #10140; amendment #10143 adds the discovered gitbox application before deletion. Amendment #10555 (git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:42168fff3d8dc623738594ff4e44a6051d6c67cd) explains that condition (2) bounds deletions, while condition (3) uses the already authorized spike smoke and its strictly cleaned disposable fixtures. The revised report states those two effects separately. Both artifacts rest directly on builder's effective promise, and the commits name the implementation request and relevant amendment. This approval closes the evidence questions; it grants no further deletion or deployment authority.\n\nArchitecture: the delivery is ordinary Git documentation and retained evidence (Gitseq layer 1), coordinated by Workroom's application and review projections (layers 5–7). Kernel, nexus and host-binding contracts are unchanged. Artroom's runtime contracts are unchanged; the deletion removes unused spike deployments while preserving the active Room/checker topology and the source needed to understand or reproduce the retired experiments.\n\nSecurity: the four deletion targets match the explicit request and amendment; the surviving application identities and bindings are accounted for. The smoke is confined to the stated spike namespace and its cleanup is recorded. Credentials in the committed result are redacted; displayed key IDs, hashes and resource names are identifiers. No unresolved defect was found in this report. I did not query the provider, run a smoke, create a credential or delete anything.\n\nSimplification: retiring unused deployments reduces the operational surface while retaining source and experimental results. The report now distinguishes inventory, runtime health and fixture cleanup, making the evidence auditable without treating an edge 404 as proof of checker health. No further report structure is needed.\n\nValidation: read the complete reporting change and recorded result, authority chain and amendments, deletion/listing evidence, surviving bindings and retained source paths. Independent npm ci, root test and root typecheck passed on revision 1 at f77ebf20; since then the only changes are this report and the new recorded JSON result, with executable source, test code, manifests and lockfile unchanged. Builder separately reports both root gates passing at this exact head. I did not redundantly rerun the unchanged runtime suites for the documentation revisions. git diff --check passes; disposable clone /tmp/artroom-checker-orphans-v3 is clean; a read-only merge-tree composition with current main 965c911a succeeds without conflict. No new runtime guard is introduced, so mutation testing does not apply to this delivery.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5d3421613b8dd1d271994db9f1bd54787e107733","binding":"assigned","head":"4dc114540ee27de276572c72505cef19020f02db","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:af1d22abb7a98c092debd3a1891ea92674644a61\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2005ed22bc76804e97ad39743edb3e4acf9c82ae\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:af1d22abb7a98c092debd3a1891ea92674644a61","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}